  "acceptance": [
    "All accepted workers in one orchestration run form a bounded batch; completed, failed and cancelled workers all settle it, and only a terminal batch receives one deterministic consolidated receipt.",
    "Completion delivery remains separate from task acceptance; the existing durable delivery owner retains pending/suspended intent while the requester is busy or paused and does not claim delivery from model text.",
    "At-least-once transport and generation fencing prevent duplicate side effects and stale deliveries from crossing reset or handoff.",
    "Restart replay, rejected/instantly failed workers, lifecycle pause/delete states, active stop and multiple independent batches have persisted evidence."
  ],
